<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy" %>
<% content_for :no_sidebar, true %>

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12">
  <h1 class="font-bold text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Last updated: August 2026</p>

  <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">1. Who we are</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Harvest is an open source project. The hosted service at this domain is operated
        by Reseau Holdings a.r.l, a company registered in Jersey under company number 136545,
        with its registered office at 1-2 Hilgrove Street, St Helier, Jersey ("we", "us", "our").
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">2. What data we collect</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">We collect the following personal data when you use the service:</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc ml-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Account information you provide, such as your name and email address.</li>
        <li>Data you enter while using the service, such as orders, tasks, and inventory records.</li>
        <li>Technical data such as IP address, browser type, and usage logs, for security and diagnostics.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">3. How we use your data</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        We use your data to provide and improve the service, authenticate you, communicate with you about
        your account (including security codes and notices), and meet our legal obligations. We do not sell
        your personal data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">4. Legal basis for processing</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Under Jersey Law, we process your data on the basis of performance of a contract (providing the service
        you signed up for), our legitimate interests (such as keeping the service secure), and, where
        applicable, your consent.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">5. Data sharing</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        We do not share your personal data with third parties except where necessary to operate the service
        (for example, hosting and email delivery providers acting on our instructions), or where required by
        law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">6. Data retention</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        We retain personal data for as long as your account is active, or as needed to provide the service
        and comply with our legal obligations. You may request deletion of your data at any time, subject to
        any legal retention requirements.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">7. Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Under Jersey Law, you have the right to access, correct, delete, or export your personal data, and to
        object to or restrict certain processing. To exercise these rights, contact us using the details
        below. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the
        <a href="https://jerseyoic.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500 dark:text-indigo-400 dark:hover:text-indigo-300">Jersey Office of the Information Commissioner</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">8. Contact us</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        If you have any questions about this policy or how we handle your data, please contact us at
        <a href="mailto:go@harvest.je" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500 dark:text-indigo-400 dark:hover:text-indigo-300">go@harvest.je</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
